WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
In 2015, Pope Francis wrote a letter to
the whole Catholic Church about caring

2
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.620
for the planet.

3
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.900
Half a century earlier, bishops from
across the world had met with the pope at

4
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.960
the Second Vatican Council.

5
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.570
Catholics take both seriously.

6
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.850
Yet one is a single letter, and
the other is a vast meeting.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.560
So who decides what Catholics believe,
and why are they trusted to do it?

8
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.970
In this mission, you'll see how Scripture,

9
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.590
Tradition and the Church's
teaching office fit together.

10
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.510
Then you'll compare two
ways the Church teaches:

11
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.170
through councils, and through popes.

12
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.120
Your mission: find out who
decides what Catholics believe,

13
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.190
and why they trust that authority.
